#1808
Edge of the Forest~
   Before you stands a huge wall of stone, sheer and gray, rising out of
the forest like the side of the world.  There is no possible way to
scale it, and it blocks the forest off completely to the west.  You
scramble up a little way but soon tire of the nearly vertical climb.
From here you can see that the forest stretches away to the east for
about three miles; beyond that there is only darkness.  A tall, sturdy
tree grows here, with branches that look easy to climb.  The forest
continues east and south.
~
